From: Emre Yavuzalp <emreyavuzalp2@gmail.com>
Subject: mips: only force vectored/EIC interrupt mode for MT SMP with a GIC

MIPS_MT_SMP force-selects CPU_MIPSR2_IRQ_VI and CPU_MIPSR2_IRQ_EI, a
Malta-era assumption that a vectored/EIC-capable interrupt controller
is present. On the EcoNet EN751221 the 34Kc advertises the VInt/VEIC
ability bits in Config3, so these options switch trap_init() to
vectored dispatch, but the SoC has no EIC: the interrupt vector number
is sampled from IPL lines nothing drives, the CPU latches RIPL=0x1f
(Cause=0x50807c00) and jumps to an uninstalled vector:

  do_default_vi -> Kernel panic: "Caught unexpected vectored interrupt."

at the very first local_irq_enable() during boot. VSMP itself has no
dependency on vectored mode: the SW0/SW1 MT IPIs from irq-mips-cpu are
plain Cause.IP bits and the classic cause-mode plat_irq_dispatch()
handles them fine, which is exactly how this platform already runs in
uniprocessor mode.

Make the two selects conditional on MIPS_GIC: the GIC is a real
EIC-capable controller and installs its vector handlers itself (this
keeps the EN7528/1004Kc+GIC configuration unchanged), while GIC-less
MT SMP systems like the EN751221 stay on cause-mode dispatch.
--- a/arch/mips/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/mips/Kconfig
@@ -2211,8 +2211,8 @@ config MIPS_MT_SMP
 	default y
 	depends on TARGET_ISA_REV > 0 && TARGET_ISA_REV < 6
 	depends on SYS_SUPPORTS_MULTITHREADING && !CPU_MICROMIPS
-	select CPU_MIPSR2_IRQ_VI
-	select CPU_MIPSR2_IRQ_EI
+	select CPU_MIPSR2_IRQ_VI if MIPS_GIC
+	select CPU_MIPSR2_IRQ_EI if MIPS_GIC
 	select SYNC_R4K
 	select MIPS_MT
 	select SMP
